    "result_text": "All changes are complete and the full suite is green (70 tests, 0 failures). Here's a summary of what I implemented for **version 2 of the owner identity**:\n\n## Version-2 identity derivation (V2 tag mixed into every identifier)\n- **New `util/IdentityVersion.java`** \u2014 a single source for the fixed `\"V2\"` tag, documenting that the tag is an identifier-only concern.\n- **`OwnerIdentity.key`** (identityKey) \u2014 now hashes `V2|telephone|email|soundex(lastName)`; still a deterministic 64-hex SHA-256, so exact-duplicate detection (409) still works.\n- **`OwnerHousehold.id`** (householdId) \u2014 now hashes `V2|normalizedLastName|postcode`; still deterministic, so same last name + postcode still converge on one household.\n- **`MemberId.of`** (memberId) \u2014 the **region code used inside the identifier** is rederived as `V2` + plain region (e.g. `V2NSW\u2026`), and HASH8 folds in the `V2` tag too. `MemberId.regionOf` stays the **plain** region.\n\nBecause each derivation folds in the `V2` tag, no value produced under version 1 recurs.\n\n## User-facing fields stay plain (no V2 tag)\n`locality` (`NSW`), `timezone` (`Australia/Sydney`) and the owner segment's derived region all continue to read `MemberId.regionOf` (the plain region), so `ownerSegment` still computes `STANDARD_METRO` etc.\n\n## Response shape\n- **openapi.yml** \u2014 added an `Identity` schema (`memberId`, `householdId`, `identityKey`), replaced the three top-level identifier fields on `Owner` with a nested `identity` object, and added a top-level integer `apiVersion` (2).\n- **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 drops the top-level identifier mappings, adds `apiVersion = 2` and a `toIdentityDto(owner)` helper that groups the three identifiers.\n\n## Audit event \u2192 schema v2\n- **`OwnerCreatedEvent`** \u2014 added `schemaVersion` (2), emitted in the JSON alongside the owner id and the version-2 memberId.\n\nThe request fields are unchanged, and the identity checks still ignore soft-deleted owners.",
